Usage: gitx <command> [options]

📂 Repository & Branch Management:
  status                                           Show repository status, branch tracking, and remote info
  fetch                                            Fetch remote branches and prune stale references
  sync                                             Sync alpha and develop with master/main
  create <branch_type> <name>                      Create a new branch from master/main
      - branch_type: feature, bugfix, hotfix, release, docs, ci, experiment
      - name: A short descriptive name for the branch
  merge <source_branch> <target_branch>            Merge one branch into another
      - source_branch: The branch to merge from
      - target_branch: The branch to merge into
  reset-branch                                     Reset current branch to remote state
      - Interactive mode with soft/hard reset options
  prune                                            Prune remote branches and delete local tracking branches
  cleanup                                          Delete merged branches
      - Prompts to confirm deletion
  orphan-branches [days]                           List/delete unmerged branches older than N days (default: 30)
  compare <branch1> <branch2>                      Compare two branches
      - branch1: The first branch to compare (optional, default: current)
      - branch2: The second branch to compare (optional, default: main)

📦 Commit & Change Management:
  ai-commit                                        Auto-generate commit message using Gemini AI
      - Uses staged files to suggest a structured commit
  commit                                           Interactive commit helper
      - Allows selecting files and entering a commit message
  amend                                            Amend the last commit message
      - Optionally enter a new commit message or edit interactively
  cherry-pick                                      Interactive cherry-pick helper
  revert                                           Revert specific commits with options
      - Interactive mode to select commits
  unstage                                          Unstage all files
      - Requires confirmation before unstaging
  stage-deleted                                    Stage all deleted files
  stage-deleted-dir <directory>                    Stage deleted files in a specific directory
      - directory: Path to the directory
  diff [output_file]                               Interactive staged diff (view/save)
  diff <start> <end> [--stat|--name-only|--patch|--details] [--to-head] [-- <path...>]
      - start/end: commit/tag OR YYYY-MM-DD YYYY-MM-DD
      - tip: date diff is inclusive (start-commit parent → end-commit)

🔍 Tracking & Reporting:
  log-file <file_path>                             View commit history and diffs for a specific file
      - file_path: Path to the file to inspect
  commit-report <start_commit..end_commit>         Generate a commit report for a commit range
  commit-report <start_date> <end_date>            Generate a commit report for a date range
      - dates: YYYY-MM-DD format
  worklog <range>|<start_date> <end_date>          Generate CSV worklog for task logs
      - range: e.g., HEAD~50..HEAD
      - dates: YYYY-MM-DD format
  summary [commit_range] [include-all] [mode]      Summarize commits + surviving code per author
  summary <start_date> <end_date> [include-all] [mode]  Same summary using date window (YYYY-MM-DD)
      - commit_range: Optional, e.g., HEAD~50
      - include-all: Optional, include all text-based files
      - mode: heavy (default, full blame) | lite (no blame, fast)
  report <start_commit> [end_commit] [file]        Generate PR and commit report
  report <start_date> <end_date> [file]              Date window (YYYY-MM-DD) → first/last commit boundaries
      - start_commit: The starting commit hash or tag
      - end_commit: The ending commit hash or tag (default: HEAD)
      - file: Output file for the report (optional)
  count-changes <start_commit> [end_commit]        Count changes (insertions, deletions) between two commits
  list-changes <branch1> <branch2>                 List files changed between two branches
      - branch1: The first branch
      - branch2: The second branch
  changelog <start_commit> <end_commit>            Generate a changelog between commits or tags
  changelog <start_date> <end_date> [file]           Date window (YYYY-MM-DD) → first/last commit boundaries
      - start_commit: The starting commit hash or tag
      - end_commit: The ending commit hash or tag

🔖 Tags & Releases:
  tag <version>                                    Tag the current branch with a version (e.g., v1.0.0)
      - version: Must follow semantic versioning (vX.Y.Z)
  latest-tag                                       Get the latest tag in the repository
  initial-commit                                   Get the initial commit hash

🗄️ Stashing & Cleanup:
  stash [subcommand]                               Manage stash operations
      - stash                      (interactive menu)
      - stash save [msg...]           Save with message (default WIP-style)
      - stash list                 List stashes
      - stash apply <n>            Apply stash@{n}
      - stash pop <n>              Pop stash@{n}
      - stash drop <n>             Drop stash@{n}
      - stash rename <n> <name...>    Rename stash@{n}
      - stash clear                Delete all stashes
  wip <save|list|pop|apply|clear>                  Opinionated WIP stash helper
  clean [--force]                                 Clean untracked files and directories
      - Interactive mode by default
      - --force: Non-interactive full clean (git clean -fd)
  large-files                                      Show the largest files in the repository
      - Prompts for the number of files to display

⚙️ Configuration & Utilities:
  add-remote <name> <url>                          Add a new remote repository
  push-remote <remote> <branch>                    Push to a specific remote branch
  pull-remote <remote> <branch>                    Pull from a specific remote branch
  config                                           Edit Git configuration (add/edit/remove keys)
  set-lf                                           Set Git to use LF line endings
  doctor                                           Run repository health checks
  hooks init                                       Install Git hook templates
  self-update                                      Update gitx to the latest version
  summarize [short]                                Repository summary (branches, tags, contributors, etc.)

🔹 Example Usages:
  gitx commit                                      # Interactive commit helper
  gitx report v1.0.0 v2.0.0                        # Generate PR and commit report
  gitx reset-branch                                # Reset current branch to match remote
  gitx compare develop main                        # Compare two branches
  gitx summary HEAD~50 include-all heavy           # Full blame, accurate surviving code
  gitx worklog 2025-01-01 2025-01-31               # CSV worklog for a month

